{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"EntityCollapse","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"singleton","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}]},{"text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"([E]) -> [E]"},{"text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","text":"The determinism requirement","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"replicated content","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other’s, and after sync ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}]},{"text":" rows are gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It must also be idempotent — ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(collapse(rows))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs as ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This is checked with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in debug builds.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"each should contain","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ID are all updated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistableModel"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","title":"PersistableModel","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","title":"SwiduxPersistence","abstract":[]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"byID(preferring:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"byID"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"preferring"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> (["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Collapses rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"choose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","title":"EntityDB","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}}}